,{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The list keeps every edge it is given, in order. Parallel edges are distinct elements, and an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge’s position is its identity, so values that belong to the edges (weights, capacities) can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"live in an array indexed the same way. Mutation follows ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Removing an edge shifts the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"later ones down and never moves an edge out of order.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices are the endpoints of the edges. An edge list has no vertex set of its own, so it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cannot hold an isolated vertex. Conversions that need one take the vertices or a vertex count"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"separately. Graph queries scan the list in O(m), because nothing is indexed."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/edgelistmodule\/edgelist"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed multigraph as an ordered list of edges, an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":" of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedEdge"},{"type":"text","text":" with graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queries."}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/EdgeListModule\/documentation\/EdgeListModule"]]},"references":{"doc://EdgeListModule/documentation/EdgeListModule/EdgeList/edgeCount":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"edgeCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"identi